# Binance spot REST responses, written from the documented formats: status
# codes, headers, the error JSON and its messages. Not captured from a live
# session; numbers are made up to fit the tests. Requests went out at server
# time 1700000000000 ms.
# - Limits and headers: https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/rest-api/limits
# - Status codes: https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/rest-api/general-api-information
# - Error codes: https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/errors
# - Rate limiters: https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/enums
# binance-exchange-info.json is an exchangeInfo body written from the
# documented example numbers (weight 6,000/min and the rest), not captured
# from a live session: `serverTime` is this file set's shared clock
# (1700000000000), not a live value. Load yours at start.

### order-ack
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
X-MBX-USED-WEIGHT-1M: 3
X-MBX-ORDER-COUNT-10S: 1
X-MBX-ORDER-COUNT-1D: 1

{"symbol":"BTCUSDT","orderId":28,"orderListId":-1,"clientOrderId":"6gCrw2kRUAF9CvJDGP16IP","transactTime":1507725176595}

### weight-429
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
Retry-After: 20
X-MBX-USED-WEIGHT-1M: 6001

{"code":-1003,"msg":"Too much request weight used; current limit is 6000 request weight per 1 MINUTE."}

### orders-429
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
Retry-After: 3
X-MBX-USED-WEIGHT-1M: 40

{"code":-1015,"msg":"Too many new orders; current limit is 100 orders per 10 SECOND."}

### orders-day-429
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
Retry-After: 30

{"code":-1015,"msg":"Too many new orders; current limit is 200000 orders per 1 DAY."}

### orders-429-unnamed
# The short message names no interval.
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
Retry-After: 3

{"code":-1015,"msg":"Too many new orders."}

### ban-418
HTTP/1.1 418 I'm a teapot
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
Retry-After: 300

{"code":-1003,"msg":"Way too much request weight used; IP banned until 1700000300000."}

### waf-403
# The WAF limit: no Retry-After, and the body is not JSON.
HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
Content-Type: text/html

<html><body>403 Forbidden</body></html>

### timestamp-400
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
X-MBX-USED-WEIGHT-1M: 4

{"code":-1021,"msg":"Timestamp for this request is outside of the recvWindow."}

### timeout-1007
# The docs give no status for -1007. A 408 is the trap: the backend may
# have taken the order, so both generic (status) and the adapter say
# Unknown, never NotRun.
HTTP/1.1 408 Request Timeout
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-1007,"msg":"Timeout waiting for response from backend server."}

### unexpected-1006
HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-1006,"msg":"An unexpected response was received from the message bus."}

### busy-1008
HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-1008,"msg":"Server is currently overloaded with other requests."}

### cancel-replace-409
HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-2021,"msg":"Order cancel-replace partially failed."}

### cancel-replace-both-failed-409
# -2022: both legs failed, nothing ran. The 409 alone is not enough.
HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-2022,"msg":"Order cancel-replace failed."}

### bad-gateway-502
HTTP/1.1 502 Bad Gateway
Content-Type: text/html

<html><body>502 Bad Gateway</body></html>

### bad-symbol-400
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{"code":-1121,"msg":"Invalid symbol."}

### bad-usage-header
# Malformed: reported as an error, never read as 0.
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8
X-MBX-USED-WEIGHT-1M: 3x

{}
